  "question": {
    "text": "On breaking a cubic solid (edge = 1 m) into fine cubic particles of edge 1 <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> , surface becomes <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>×</mo><mn>100000</mn></math> . The value of n is?"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "10.00",
  "solution": {
    "text": "For a cube of dimension <math><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>)</mo></math> , the surface area<br /><math><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>×</mo><mn>6</mn></math> faces<br /><math><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><msup><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br />The volume <math> <mrow>  <mtext>=</mtext><mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><mtext>1</mtext><mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><msup>   <mtext>m</mtext>   <mtext>3</mtext>  </msup>  <mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><mtext>&#x00D7;</mtext><mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><msup>   <mrow>    <mfenced>     <mrow>      <mfrac>       <mrow>        <mtext>1&#x03BC;m</mtext></mrow>       <mrow>        <msup>         <mrow>          <mtext>10</mtext></mrow>         <mrow>          <mo>&#x2212;</mo><mtext>6</mtext></mrow>        </msup>        <mtext>m</mtext></mrow>      </mfrac>      </mrow>    </mfenced></mrow>   <mtext>3</mtext>  </msup>  </mrow></math><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>18</mn></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><msup><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math><br />For <math><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>18</mn></mrow></msup></math> cubes of dimension <math><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>)</mo></math> , the total surface area<br /><math><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>18</mn></mrow></msup><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>×</mo><mn>6&nbsp;</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>18</mn></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><msup><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br />On breaking, the surface area becomes<br /><math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>18</mn></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><msup><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><msup><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math> times<br />= 1000000 times<br />Hence n = 10"
  }
